# A real environment file carries the bearer token, and opend.conf may carry
# the moomoo login. Only the templates belong in the repository. The negation
# is defensive rather than load-bearing — `*.env` does not match a name ending
# in `.env.example` — and it must stay below the pattern it exempts, because
# git honours the last matching rule.
*.env
!*.env.example
opend.conf
